source: crates/leptoskit_cli/tests/snapshots.rs
expression: "normalize(&stdout(&output), &scratch.path)"
---
Builds the project for a platform

Usage: leptoskit build [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --app-target <NAME>              Select a named target from the root leptoskit.toml
      --release                        Build in release mode
      --platform <PLATFORM>            The platform to build; defaults to the configuration's
      --optimize <OPTIMIZE>            How hard to optimize a release client for size, `fast` or `smallest`; defaults to `bundle.optimize`. Needs `--release`
      --out <OUT>                      The output directory, relative to the project root [default: dist]
      --unsigned                       Build the release without signing it: an APK or app no store takes, for measuring or testing. Without it, an Android, Quest, or iOS release is signed, or not built
      --export-method <EXPORT_METHOD>  Who an iOS release's `.ipa` is for: app-store-connect, ad-hoc, or development. Defaults to `native.ios.export-method`
      --build-number <BUILD_NUMBER>    The release's build number: Android's `versionCode`, and iOS's `CFBundleVersion`. Each store upload needs a higher one
  -h, --help                           Print help
  -V, --version                        Print version
